#====================================================================
# E318 Draft - fixed-target compiler validation without ABI mixing
#====================================================================

id:                     E356
trigger_tool:           conan|chibicc|test_package|ohos-test-runner|qemu
phase:                  build|testing|source
error_signature:        make: inaccessible or not found|Read-only file system|features.h:.*no expression|bits/alltypes.h:.*expected an expression|in eval_const_expr: no expression|in primary: expected an expression|in paste: invalid preprocessing token|cannot open file: No such file or directory

severity:               2
category:               compiler, testing, abi, path-c, source-provenance
match_keywords:         chibicc, compiler package, x86-64 output, OHOS armv8, high difficulty, source-owned closure, native glibc execution, target header blocker, exact XFAIL, blocking XPASS, ABI mismatch, R39
title:                  Validate fixed-target compilers without mixing target ABIs

root_cause:             chibicc/1.0.24.1 builds and runs as an OHOS/armv8 executable but unconditionally generates x86-64 code. Upstream tests link and execute the generated x86-64 programs, so the armv8 worker cannot provide executable evidence. Injecting OHOS/armv8 libc headers mixes target ABIs. A musl x86-64 environment is also insufficient for this fork because its self-hosted source assumes glibc header and linker layouts; native execution evidence therefore requires a matching glibc x86-64 userspace.
affected_scope:         Compiler packages whose generated-code target architecture or target libc differs from the OHOS worker environment.

verification_cmd:       CI_PACKAGES="archives/c/chibicc/1.0.24.1" zsh ci/conan/build_and_test.sh; CHIBICC_SOURCE_DIR=<verified-source> CHIBICC_RESULTS_DIR=<results> bash test_package/test_native_x86_64.sh

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           two-plane-fixed-target-validation
rec_description:        Keep the OHOS/armv8 package gate fail-closed at the source-owned compile boundary, then run the complete upstream stage1 and genuinely self-hosted stage2 suites in a matching glibc x86-64 environment. Require exact source inventories, per-case terminal states, both driver suites, all 13 stage2 self-hosted objects, and explicit pass and execution denominators. Preserve deterministic XFAIL, target-header blockers, compile failures, runtime failures, and missing dependency blockers as non-PASS outcomes.
rec_command:            CHIBICC_SOURCE_DIR=<verified-source> CHIBICC_RESULTS_DIR=<results> CHIBICC_JOBS=4 bash test_package/test_native_x86_64.sh
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-test-package-and-native-runner

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      external-glibc-x86_64-runner
fallback_description:   Run the committed native harness in QEMU TCG or equivalent x86-64 Linux virtualization when no physical x86-64 worker is available. Verify the guest is glibc based and retain the result TSV and logs.
fallback_command:       make LDFLAGS= test && make LDFLAGS= test-stage2
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          external-test-environment

forbid_1_pattern:       merge OHOS armv8 libc or dependency headers into chibicc x86-64 code generation
forbid_1_reason:        Header declarations describe the worker ABI while chibicc emits another ABI; parse success would not prove a valid target build.
forbid_1_consequence:   Compile counts overstate validity and can hide ABI-level incompatibility.

forbid_2_pattern:       classify every cannot-open-file diagnostic as target-header-blocked
forbid_2_reason:        Missing local fixtures, path regressions, and undeclared dependencies would be silently accepted.
forbid_2_consequence:   The test package can pass while source-owned tests were not compiled.

forbid_3_pattern:       claim blocked inventory, compile-only coverage, or XFAIL as upstream executable pass
forbid_3_reason:        Inventory coverage does not execute generated x86-64 programs, and XFAIL remains a measured non-PASS result.
forbid_3_consequence:   PR evidence violates non-weakening and test-accounting requirements.

forbid_4_pattern:       accept only an aggregate failure count, allow XPASS silently, or call a hybrid stage2 build self-hosted
forbid_4_reason:        Aggregate counts can conceal replacement regressions; XPASS means the inventory is stale; host-object fallback does not validate self-hosting.
forbid_4_consequence:   Regressions and bootstrap failures can be mislabeled as successful validation.

doc_file:               drafts/E318-draft-chibicc-path-c-assembly-validation.md
last_updated:           2026-08-14
source_event:           PR #4710 chibicc/1.0.24.1 high-difficulty review and executable-coverage remediation

